From 689674ad60c5a74d3795a71399734113f4af6758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:18:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] :bug: Give detached buffers aliasable temporary backing

A detached buffer imports its temporary allocation without copying before
it detaches. Linux DMA-BUF export needs file-backed pages, so request the
existing aliasable allocation contract already used by detached heaps.
Keep anonymous reservations, fixed overwrites, remaps and release order.

Add an opt-in test VM model that refuses aliases of ordinary reservations,
then check the temporary's shared bytes and lifetime through that model.
Add a native Linux regression for size seals and the file descriptor's
lifetime through its last mapped view.

On Linux each temporary now consumes a memfd and inherits the existing
allocator's fatal file-creation, truncate and seal failure behavior. This
is a deliberate resource-exhaustion difference from anonymous allocation.

Validation: 38 affected core tests pass. The new core regression fails
when the allocation call is reverted to allocate_anywhere. Native Linux
VM/remap tests could not run: rustc compiling the local metal2vulkan
candidate was killed by SIGKILL twice, including at one job without debug
information. No GPU tests or guest boot were performed.
